==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*5 [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*4 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Alpacky]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[LeMurr]]s spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is the point of the dojos where having all alien crystals from [[Into the Future]] will be necessary, as without them the Ursamajors will be buffed to tremendous levels and will be too much for the players to handle.

Use the starting peons to stall and get money, as you won't have much after triggering the base. When they come out, kill the Ursamajors quickly to make sure they don't stack up. The LeMurrs are single target, so adequate meatshielding will be enough to prevent them from being an issue, although you should kill them before they start stacking up. The Alpacky isn't much of a threat, just as a way to prevent you from pushing too far. Once the LeMurrs and both Ursamajors are dead, you are free to kill Alpacky and beat the stage.

==Hints==
This hint only appears as a defeat message that is given after losing the stage.
*This stage is super tough to clear without<br>Superior Treasures from all Into the Future<br>chapters. Use Treasure Radars to <br>guarantee you collect the best Treasures!

